Here are the limits of each function at $x=-1$, according to the graphs:

$\begin{align}
&\blueD{\displaystyle\lim_{x\to -1}h(x)=2}
\\\\
&\maroonD{\displaystyle\lim_{x\to -1}f(x)=4}
\end{align}$

Now we can find $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to -1}\Big(h(x)f(x)\Big)$ using the fact that the limit of a product of functions is the product of the individual limits:

$\displaystyle\lim_{x\to -1}\Big(h(x)f(x)\Big)=\lim_{x\to -1}h(x)\cdot \lim_{x\to -1}f(x)$
